u-boot-spacemit (1.0.5-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Split the single binary package into two independent packages:
    - u-boot-spl-spacemit: the SPL/FSBL chain (FSBL.bin, bootinfo blobs
      and the default U-Boot environment);
    - u-boot-spacemit: U-Boot proper packaged as a FIT image
      (u-boot.itb) bundling U-Boot and the device trees.
  * Factor the boot-device detection logic out of the postinst into a
    shared helper (spacemit-boot-device.sh) shipped by both packages at
    package-private paths. Each postinst sources its own copy and writes
    only the components it owns: the SPL package flashes bootinfo, FSBL
    and the environment; the proper package flashes u-boot.itb (still
    skipped under UEFI, as before).
  * Translate all packaging comments to English (rules, postinst,
    helper).
  * Broaden the SpacemiT K3/X100 platform detection to accept any of:
    the "Spacemit(R) X100" model string in /proc/cpuinfo (older
    kernels), the "spacemit,x100" uarch line in /proc/cpuinfo (newer
    kernels), or "spacemit,k3" in /proc/device-tree/compatible.
  * Drop opensbi Build-Depends: the K3 build never consumes OpenSBI 
    (CONFIG_BINMAN is not set and the FIT ITS bundles only 
    u-boot-nodtb.bin with the device trees). OpenSBI is a separate
    runtime payload loaded by SPL from its own partition, so add
    opensbi-spacemit as a Recommends on u-boot-spl-spacemit instead.

 -- Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>  Fri, 24 Jul 2026 11:25:34 +0200

